# Chaperone backend configuration.
#
# Copy to server/.env and fill in whichever providers you have — you need at
# least one. The backend reads this file (its working directory is server/),
# not any .env in the repo root.
#
# With more than one configured, the engine is chosen in this order:
#   Custom -> Claude -> OpenAI -> Gemini
# Pin a specific one in the app under Settings -> Model engine.
#
# You can also leave this file empty and paste keys into Settings instead; the
# app writes them back here.

# --- Claude (Anthropic) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# --- OpenAI ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Gemini (Google) ---
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Any other OpenAI-compatible provider ---
# One slot for a provider that isn't one of the three above. Most of them speak
# the OpenAI dialect, so only the base URL differs -- no code change needed.
#   DeepSeek    https://api.deepseek.com/v1          deepseek-chat
#   Kimi        https://api.moonshot.cn/v1           moonshot-v1-8k
#   GLM         https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4 glm-4
#   Qwen        https://dashscope.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
#   OpenRouter  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   Ollama      http://localhost:11434/v1            (any local model)
# Check the provider's own docs for the current URL and model names.
# All four are required for this slot to activate.
# CUSTOM_API_KEY=
# CUSTOM_BASE_URL=
# CUSTOM_MODEL=
# CUSTOM_LABEL=

# Note: the pipeline leans on function calling. Endpoints that only partly
# implement OpenAI tool calls may connect fine and then stall in the agent loop.

# --- Optional ---
# Where to look for skill definitions.
# SKILLS_PATH=
# Node's fetch ignores the system proxy; set this if your machine needs one.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
